  "category" : "Students and Teachers",
  "createdAt" : 1731968952,
  "description" : "This dataset contains MCAS Alternate Assessment (MCAS-Alt) results by percent of students at each achievement level by grade and subject since 2017.\n\nThe MCAS-Alt evaluates the achievement of students with significant cognitive disabilities. It is offered in every subject and grade for which a statewide academic assessment is offered. MCAS-Alt results are reported based on alternate academic achievement standards, rather than on the grade-level achievement standards used for reporting standard MCAS testing results. For more information about the MCAS-Alt, see the Background section included in the Department of Elementary and Secondary Education's annual <a href=\"https://www.doe.mass.edu/mcas/alt/results.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">State Summary of Participation and Achievement</a> document.\n\nStudents with significant cognitive disabilities are required by law to participate in statewide academic assessments and to be counted in the achievement results of all assessed students. Only students who meet the eligibility criteria for a student with the most significant cognitive disabilities may be assigned to take the MCAS-Alt. For more information about the participation of students with disabilities in MCAS, please visit the <a href=\"http://www.doe.mass.edu/mcas/participation.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Student Participation</a> page on DESE's website.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/mcas_alt.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MCAS-Alt Achievement Results</a>",
